# 🌦️ WeatherMcpServer

A local [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) (MCP) server, built on .NET 9,
that gives any MCP-compatible AI client (Claude Desktop, VS Code + Copilot Chat, Claude Code, etc.)
a real-time weather tool — current conditions and a daily forecast for **any place in the world**,
by name.

Powered by [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/) — free, global coverage, no API key required.

```
"What's the weather in Hyderabad?"
   → get_forecast("Hyderabad")
   → Forecast for Hyderabad, India:
     Current temperature: 28.1°C
     2026-08-18: High 30.1°C, Low 24.3°C, Rain chance 40%
     ...
```

## ✨ Features

- 🌍 **Global coverage** — resolves any city/place name via Open-Meteo's geocoding API, not just US locations
- 🔌 **Zero config** — no API keys, no secrets, works out of the box
- 📡 **Standard MCP over stdio** — drop-in compatible with any MCP host
- 🧱 **Minimal footprint** — one tool, ~100 lines of code, easy to read and extend

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- [.NET 9](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/)
- [ModelContextProtocol](https://www.nuget.org/packages/ModelContextProtocol) — official C# MCP SDK
- [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/) forecast + geocoding APIs

